@startuml alert-states
!include _style.puml

title State of the alert of one machine

state Normal
state Warning
state Critical
state Recovered

[*] --> Normal

Normal --> Warning : temperature at or above the warning threshold,\nor rise above the limit over a full window
Normal --> Critical : temperature at or above the critical threshold
Warning --> Critical : temperature at or above the critical threshold
Warning --> Recovered : temperature below the warning threshold\nless the margin
Critical --> Recovered : temperature below the warning threshold\nless the margin
Recovered --> Normal : next reading, no condition met
Recovered --> Warning : next reading at or above the warning threshold\nor rise above the limit
Recovered --> Critical : next reading at or above the critical threshold

note right of Warning
  An alert that a rise caused closes only after the rate
  has stayed below the limit for a full window.
  A critical alert stays critical until it closes.
end note

note right of Recovered
  The state of the reading at which the alert closed.
  It lasts for one reading.
end note

@enduml
